{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4Yh2JSPr8wYHMPHXDgm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GTTkK17tKT4WwexLJuNDpY","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 15/32: review of the .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py deletion hunk (v1.4.3-rc.1..0e687e3c)\n\nSCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD\nThis piece is only removed lines from .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py. It covers:\n- the tail of the replay/pattern/threat-model emitters and iter_events;\n- the whole emit_generic dispatcher;\n- the session/prompt/output emitters;\n- the audit-tokens allowlist and emitters;\n- the codex/grok/council, pair-rail, directory-added, notification, night-mode and learning-loop enums and allowlists;\n- the ledger, compaction, context-pressure and subagent allowlists;\n- the context-pressure marker logic (should_emit_context_pressure, the sharded GC, clear_context_pressure_marker);\n- the start of the typed emitters.\nUnder PLAN-197 / ADR-202 this code moves into .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/. I judged the deletion against where the code now lives in the candidate tree.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED AGAINST THE CANDIDATE TREE\n1. emit_generic.\n   - Every elif branch removed here comes back in the same order: 34 in generic_dispatch_01.py, 45 in _02, 45 in _03, 28 in _04, and 20 plus the passthrough in _05.\n   - The passthrough is still checked last, after every explicit branch (generic_dispatch_05.py:352). Default-deny is still {\"action\": action} plus a breadcrumb (generic_dispatch_05.py:375-377).\n   - Each branch ends with state[\"event\"] = event; return True. I counted 3 markers per branch in every file, so no branch writes the unscrubbed dict.\n   - The three branches that dropped the whole event (persona_coverage_synthesized, tier_policy_loader_fallback_observed, audit_producer_path_pollution_detected) still return None, so no stub event is written (generic_dispatch_01.py:440-450, generic_dispatch_03.py:96-126).\n   - I compared the security-relevant value coercions line by line and they match: ledger_entry_rejected, settings_tamper_detected, salt_rotation_registered, pair_rail_case/review_expected, credential_override_late_set_ignored, swarm_paused_owner_absent, mcp_injection_finding, session_memory_delta_observed, the learning-loop branches, and codex/grok/council.\n   - The fail-open wrappers on the task_route_key_dropped and reality_ledger_key_dropped side-emits are kept.\n2. Enum and constant values match the removed text: _LEDGER_GATE_FAMILIES/REASONS, _LEDGER_ID_RE, _SETTINGS_TAMPER_CLASSES, _TOOL_CALL_LIFECYCLE_TOOL_NAME_ENUM, _GIT_HOOK_BYPASS_FLAG_CLASSES, _PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX, the context-pressure bucket/TTL/GC/wall-budget constants, and the regex shape gates.\n3. Context-pressure code: context_pressure.py is the same text, including the symlink protections (O_EXCL, O_NOFOLLOW, a random tmp name, mode 0600) and the fail-open re-arm. Every free name it reads is in some part's __all__. I checked the compaction.py exports: _GC_MARKER_WALL_BUDGET_S, _CONTEXT_PRESSURE_STATE_BASENAME and the SID/TTL/GC constants. So the GC path cannot raise a NameError that its (OSError, TypeError, ValueError) guard would miss.\n4. Moved-code mechanics (checklist item 4):\n   - install() (_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48) rebinds every part function onto the facade's globals. Monkeypatching audit_emit._write_event, _breadcrumb, emit_generic and similar still takes effect.\n   - global _FALLBACK_NOTIFIED resolves to the facade.\n   - Locks stay in the facade (audit_emit.py:483-484), so deepcopy never touches them.\n   - All 37 part files have `from __future__ import annotations`. Typing names such as List, Tuple and Iterator, which the facade does not import, appear only in annotations.\n   - Module-level re.compile calls are in parts that import re themselves.\n   - iter_events stays a lazy generator through the SimpleNamespace indirection (audit_emit.py:455-461). Only replay.py exports it.\n   - The spool-writer forensic emitter and exit-handler hookup at import time is kept (audit_emit.py:486-496).\n5. Python 3.9 and standard library: FunctionType(code, globals, name, argdefs, closure) and __kwdefaults__ work on 3.9. I found no match statements, zip(strict=), runtime X|Y unions or third-party imports in the parts.\n6. Condition 5, for this file: check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 lists `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*`. All 13 lines the condition names are present at :309-340.\n7. Condition 7 holds for audit_emit: the path is unchanged and the logic now lives in _lib/_audit_emit_parts/.\n8. Adopter delivery: scripts/install.sh:1522-1541 installs each entry under hooks/_lib/ with install_one (cp -R for directories), so the new subpackage is copied.\n\nNo declared condition is contradicted by this payload, and I found no P0.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1: decoy branches defeat the structural guard tests.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:473-480.\n- Scenario: the facade's emit_generic has `if action == \"tool_call_lifecycle_recorded\": _dispatch_generic(...)` and `if action == \"settings_tamper_detected\": _dispatch_generic(...)`. Both do exactly what the fall-through line does. They exist only so that inspect.getsource(audit_emit.emit_generic) still contains those comparisons, which .claude/hooks/tests/test_tool_lifecycle.py:541-563 and .claude/scripts/tests/test_ceo_boot_tamper_tripwires.py:521-525 require. The real scrub branches are generic_dispatch_04.py:62 and :159. If either is deleted or broken, those tests stay green. Today's behaviour is correct, and a regression would fall to default-deny (fields lost, not leaked), so this is test honesty, not a leak.\n- Minimal fix: remove the decoys and point the tests at the real branch, either by inspecting _apply_generic_group_04 or, better, by calling audit_emit.emit_generic with a forbidden field and asserting it is dropped and the enums are coerced.\n\nP2-2: dead duplicate action registry.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py:7-16, with actions_core.py (234 names) and actions_extended.py (97 names).\n- Scenario: these define a second 331-name _KNOWN_ACTIONS, but the install() roster does not include them (audit_emit.py:415-452). The runtime registry is the literal at audit_emit.py:45-377, which is also what _reality_ledger_parts/audit_actions.py:29-39 reads first. A maintainer who registers a new action in actions_core.py, which env-inventory.json also points at, gets no runtime effect. The action is then dropped as unknown, the same silent-drop class as the S76 skill_bootstrap_used regression.\n- Minimal fix: delete actions*.py, or add a parity test pinning them equal to the facade literal.\n\nP2-3: unknown-action breadcrumb lost repr escaping.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/generic_dispatch_05.py:363.\n- Scenario: the removed code logged f\"emit_generic: unknown action {action!r}\". The new code logs \"unknown audit action dropped: %s\" % action. An action string carrying a newline or control characters now writes raw into the audit-log.errors sidecar, which is not chained, so lines can be forged there. Callers pass constants, so exposure is low.\n- Minimal fix: use %r, and keep the old message text for anyone grepping for it.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Every branch, enum, constant and fail-open path removed from audit_emit.py in this payload comes back unchanged and in the same order in _lib/_audit_emit_parts/, bound to the facade's globals so patch points still work, Python 3.9 compatible and standard-library only; condition 5's kernel line for the package is present, and the only findings are three P2 follow-ups, with no P0 and no false condition."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3309,"cache_read_input_tokens":233227,"cache_c